# Local development secrets (copy to .dev.vars and fill in real values).
#
# The Worker needs NONE: its bindings are in wrangler.jsonc, its vars too, and a user's
# credentials arrive by pairing into KV. This file exists because `wrangler dev` expects the
# mechanism to be there.
#
# Do not put tooling keys here. `wrangler types` folds this file into the generated `Env`, so
# anything in it becomes a *required* member of the Worker's config — and `pnpm check` then
# fails for every test fixture that builds an Env. Tooling secrets belong in `.probe.env`.
